# None is rejected as a parallelization core budget

Core budgets accept an integer or null; the legacy `None` spelling is rejected
before the source program executes.

>>> source
@config { parallelization: { cores: None } }

<<< stdout

<<< stderr
eck: invalid value for configuration `parallelization.cores`: parallelization.cores must be a nonnegative integer worker count or null at Span { start: 36, end: 40 }

<<< exit
1
